class:: ViewCentralOV
summary:: A simple example implementation of a facade/coordinator for ViewCentral and ViewCentralModel
categories:: gui>views
related:: Classes/ViewCentralModel, Classes/ViewCentral, Classes/Window


description::
ViewCentralOV shows how to build a container class that coordinate ViewCentralModel and ViewCentral. It is a  optional simple example of a design pattern implementatation rather a dependency for ViewCentralModel or ViewCentral.

ViewCentralOV demonstrated:

list::
## Method forwarding using link::#-doesNotUnderstand::
## Window recreation while maintaining model state
## Notification forwarding from model to observers
::

note::
ViewCentralOV is intended as a template to use or adapt for other container classes.
::

classmethods::

method:: new
Creates a new ViewCentralOV instance that manages both a model and view.

argument:: dims
An array of two Integers [width, height] specifying the view dimensions. Passed to the model.

argument:: margins
Margins in pixels. Can be a single Integer, an array of two [horiz, vert], or an array of four [left, top, right, bottom]. Passed to the model.

argument:: usrViewBool
Boolean indicating whether to use a UserView (true) or a regular View (false). Passed to the model.

argument:: win
An optional Window instance. If nil, a new Window is created.

instancemethods::

method:: window
Returns the current Window instance.

method:: model
Returns the ViewCentralModel instance.

method:: view
Returns the ViewCentral instance.

method:: recreateView
Recreates the view while maintaining model state.
argument:: win
An optional Window instance. If nil, a new Window is created.

discussion::
This method demonstrates how to handle window recreation. It creates a new ViewCentral instance with the same model, preserving state.

method:: isViewClosed
Returns true if the view doesn't exist or its window is closed.

method:: ensureViewExists
Ensures a valid view exists, recreates it if necessary. Example of a "self healing" design.

method:: contentView
Returns the content view.

discussion::
This is a convenience method, providing direct access to the View or UserView

code::
// instead of
v = ViewCentralOV.new;
Button(v.view.view, Rect(10, 10, 100, 30));

// convenience method:
Button(v.contentView, Rect(10, 50, 100, 30));
::

method:: refresh
Refreshes the content view to display any changes.

method:: autoRecreate
Get or set whether views should be automatically recreated when methods are called on closed views.

argument:: bool
Boolean value. If false (default), an error is posted. If true, closed views are automatically recreated when methods are called.

See examples below.

method:: doesNotUnderstand
Delegates calls to undefined methods and forwards them to the appropriate class instance (model / view).

argument:: selector
The name of the method that was called but not found in this class.

argument:: ... args
The arguments that were passed to the undefined method (collected using SuperCollider's variable argument syntax code::...args::).

discussion::
A part of the Facade pattern implementation which is invoked when a method not defined in ViewCentralOV is called.

method:: update
Forwards notifications from the model to this object's dependents.
argument:: obj
The object that sent the notification (typically the model).
argument:: what
A symbol indicating what changed.
argument:: value
The new value or additional information about the change.

examples::

code::


// Simple example with all arguments specified

// Create a custom window first
w = Window.new.front;

// Create ViewCentralOV with all arguments
// |dims, margins, usrViewBool, win|
v = ViewCentralOV.new([450, 340], [30, 20],  true, w)


(
// Use forwarded methods mechanism
v.winName_("ViewCentralOV Example");
v.viewCol_(Color.grey(0.9));
v.marginCol_(Color.yellow(0.9));
v.resizeWin(500, 400);
v.winCol_(Color.blue);
// Add content to the view
v.contentView.drawFunc = {
Pen.fillColor = Color.blue;
Pen.fillOval(Rect(150, 100, 100, 100));
Pen.stringCenteredIn(
    "ViewCentralOV example",
    Rect(0, 0, v.contentView.bounds.width, 30)
);
};
v.contentView.refresh;
)

// Close the window
v.close;

// Automatic recreation
v = ViewCentralOV.new;
v.autoRecreate_(true);

v.close;

// Window automatically recreates
v.marginCol_(Color.yellow);
::